[Music]  hello my name is orlando louis pardo  i'm a chess instructor and i have been  working with the chess club and  scholastic center since  2019 i teach scouts and  also elementary secondary and colleges  yeah when i started i was traveling all  around the city  from school to school different  neighborhoods different different areas  of the city that i didn't know  i am from havana cuba so i have been  living in san luis for  only four years and it was a way of also  understanding  the city and suddenly this year after  the social distances and everything that  started well it has been very different  because basically i'm at my place  every day facing the same computer but  still trying to bring to those kids  the imagination creativity the desire to  play  to understand the game zoom up allows us  to do a video conference a video call  so i'm able to start talking to the kids  all of the kids can see me i can see  them  then i can share the screen so i can  explain  in a with a chess playing  website like liches or chess.com  especially leeches is the one that we're  using  i explain to them a number of notions  and they can only  listen and watch what i'm doing but then  i invite them to share their  screens too so they can also explain to  me back or  discuss some questions that they may  have but then  i invite them to play a tournament in  real time they cannot play  using the zoom app you cannot play chess  by using skype for example you know  so we need to also shift this  internet the browser tab to the  liches.org  website they need to have an account  created  on alice.org it's a safe website but  you can even create special accounts for  children  and then once that you have an account  everybody is logged in we go to a second  tab  i keep sharing the screen and then there  we start playing a tournament  so they are we are really using two  internet  tools zoom and then liches and we are  playing on real time while i keep  talking  giving some instructions some tutoring  games guiding comments  jokes uh during the tournament so  they and they at the same time they talk  to me during the tournament sometimes a  little noisy and then i say please  respectfully muting everybody so that we  could concentrate in the game  because they but they are at the same  time they are learning you know to be  polite to be gentle with it it would be  nice with the opponent  they they learn very early on even if  they get frustrated when they lose a  game say  good game good game next time we'll be  different yes but good game right now  and and  wishing each other good luck we want to  win  but we want to win playing chess we the  opponent we need the opponent otherwise  we wouldn't be able to play  we wouldn't be able to win we wouldn't  be able to lose or to make a  hard-fought draw so the idea that we  need to reach out for others  that the the other person is there maybe  in our living room  and we need to respect each other and  keep civility  the conversation going on i'm very  frustrated today i lost my first three  games  still i'm happy we are in a community  next day maybe we'll be better  and if it's not going better it's  because you're doing something wrong and  if you're doing something wrong we can  work on that  to try to make it not wrong anymore to  try to make it right so it's a very  nice and constructive idea and  use the internet to teach chess and  learn chess  only in other areas of internet maybe  there is a lot of  battleground going on but in the case of  chess the battleground  goes to the chess pieces no and then  people to people is a nice engagement  i feel that when i am teaching online  and also learning online from my  students  [Music]

